    "turn_text": "isn't great. You know, they have bigger plans, but certainly one of the things the Democrats have done successfully, and we've now, and we try and replicate this for Republicans, is find those state and local leaders who already have that footprint. Like, for example, in Iowa, Ashley Henson, who's a new freshman representative, was a state senator already. Nicole Malliotakis in Staten Island also was a state senator or state rep, and so that made them more effective candidates, particularly since they were challenging incumbents. So that's kind of what we look for, you know, a view pack or winning for women, both of the groups, I'm on their board when we're trying to find women. But, you know, over the past, you know, several cycles, obviously, Trump has made that whole dynamic difficult, certainly, you know, for the class of 18, the women got wiped out. which is really what inspired a lot of them to come back, you know, women to run again, people like young Kim actually was on the ballot in 18, and then she ran again in 20, you know, she's really a model candidate because",
