    "turn_text": "What type of organization and networking is in place is being put in place to elevate the women, especially who are our best representative of the Republican narrative and sort of philosophy as opposed to what we've seen happen with Trumpism. And to really kind of build that bench, as you said, which has always been a big deal for me as a former party official, is if you don't have a bench, then you're not ready to play. Because the moment one of your players go down, how do you replace them? Where do you go? You've always got to think about building that. So it's refreshing on the one hand, to see so many women looking to run. But it is potentially concerning on the other if they are running to represent Donald Trump and Trumpism as opposed to those values that you and I, both as candidate and as elected officials, have always espoused, you know, in articulating the values and the principles that distinguish us from our democratic friends. And that's part of the healthy part of the debate around some of these things.",
