    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51078.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 192,
    "turn_text": "And we take them, the whole idea is to take them into the workplace, whether it's capital one, was wonderful and had us come over and the girls got to, these high school young women got to visit and meet all the leading women they had there. Of course, we bring them to Congress. Donna Edwards pairs up with me and does it. Nice. Congresswoman from Maryland. The ANOVA hospital took us all through their new cancer wing and we got to meet with women doctors who are doing this and so It's just exciting to put Sheila Johnson, the first African-American billionaire in the world, came in with our young women. So it's my passion project too. And that's why I like whether it's helping get women elected or having these next generation of women leaders. start thinking of themselves as leaders at a young age. It's something that, and one of the things we do with the young girls is we do things on human trafficking, we do things on sexual harassment, and we try and introduce them to the whole world in that space so that they aren't victimized in their careers and hear from people and on those kind of issues too so that they can step into the whole world of women and leadership in a more confident way.",
